      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Object Storage**\n\nOkay, I'm zeroing in on an object storage provider. Given the user's needs, AWS S3 is looking like the most practical choice. I'm starting to think about how to structure the code so the S3 dependency is clearly identified.\n\n\n**Defining the File Structure**\n\nI've decided to start by creating the `presigned_download.py` file. I'm building out a function within it that will handle the URL generation, taking the bucket, object, and expiration time as inputs. I'll be using `boto3` to interact with AWS S3, ensuring this dependency is clear in the code's structure.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820008126,
          "start": 1789820005920
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b995ee20001cSk3aCHFKVzZzU",
      "message_id": "msg_0b995e99d0017mlmH5Yqmpe7FZ",
      "session_id": "ses_f466a1676ffeOnRShykgUGnhzl",
      "time_created": 1789820005920,
      "time_updated": 1789820008126
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "xtMYFKY06UbvSQJI",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef create_presigned_download_url(bucket_name: str, object_name: str, expiration: int = 3600):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a time-limited presigned URL for downloading a stored object from AWS S3.\n\n    Args:\n        bucket_name (str): The name of the S3 bucket.\n        object_name (str): The key of the object to download.\n        expiration (int): The number of seconds the presigned URL is valid for.\n                          Defaults to 3600 seconds (1 hour).\n\n    Returns:\n        str: The presigned URL if successful, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    s3_client = boto3.client(\n        's3',\n        aws_access_key_id=os.environ.get(\"AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID\"),\n        aws_secret_access_key=os.environ.get(\"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\"),\n        aws_session_token=os.environ.get(\"AWS_SESSION_TOKEN\")\n    )\n    try:\n        response = s3_client.generate_presigned_url(\n            'get_object',\n            Params={'Bucket': bucket_name, 'Key': object_name},\n            ExpiresIn=expiration\n        )\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error generating presigned URL: {e}\")\n        return None\n    return response\n",
            "filePath": "presigned_download.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
