      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Target Provider**\n\nI've decided to target AWS S3 as the object storage provider. Now, my focus is on ensuring its clear identification within the Python code I'm developing.\n\n\n**Implementing the Core Logic**\n\nI'm now fully immersed in constructing the `upload_object.py` script. The foundation includes a function that accepts file paths or byte streams, bucket names, and object keys. I've integrated `boto3` to interact seamlessly with AWS S3, and I'm ensuring all the necessary AWS-specific configurations are in place to make the provider choice clear and unambiguous within the script.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789820003517,
          "start": 1789820000989
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b995dadd0016qmuH6DoqKFJfg",
      "message_id": "msg_0b995d58b001qnjGAbDLc0zSpV",
      "session_id": "ses_f466a2afaffegkClYXkjvOv1DO",
